Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:17:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] Resolution: the fork-main conflicts of this series on
 e4245f3c1

The series was resolved once as a merge of fork main e4245f3c1 into the v0.1 stack
(ceb9e1f7a + 39 patches). Linearised onto e4245f3c1 without 0012 (#927) and 0013
(#1002), both now in fork main, the conflicting hunks of the other patches were
taken from the picked side; this patch brings in the merge-time resolutions (it
replaces v0.1's resolution on ceb9e1f7a), so the full series gives the merged tree.

Decisions (docs/rebase.md has the list):
- #927: fork main's newer revision kept everywhere (d16 accesses name a place only
  where every access does; a run-time pick names none); our older copies of its
  tests and of its descriptor-data condition (now in descriptor_data.rs) dropped.
- Split dispatches (#993, USER_GROUP_BASE) kept over upstream's spread across z
  (USER_DISPATCH_SPREAD, VIctory #2312); #646's USER_DISPATCH_THREADS (0x106) and
  DispatchX thread counts wired onto the split path; `is_spread` is a split dispatch.
- #995's indirect clamp kept (record_clamp_as, rec_* constants); fork main's clamp
  window and gather segments run on it (same six constants, bit 16 read as
  rec_has_count), VICTORY_CLAMP_LEAN through record_clamp_with(.., lean).
- VICTORY_DIRTY_4K not taken: #995's fine pages (VICTORY_FINE_PAGES, `Written`)
  copy only the written 4 KiB pages already; its journal and hook left out.
- VICTORY_PAGE_WRITES: fork main's default 1|2|8 and bit 8 (the black-face fix);
  "1" stays guards + slots.
- Upstream #3198 (host textures retried when the card had no room): Result<_,
  NoTexture> on our host_desc / small-texture split.
- VICTORY_WAVE_WIDE_ONLY (WAVE_WIDE_HERE) selects Wide::Any in our wave-wide modes.
- #1112 / #646 partial-thread masks added to the paired form's ballots and the
  double sums (float64.rs).
- Tests: HostShader initialisers of the #854/#993 and #1489 tests given half_views
  (and root views), test-only Flight / Card fields, compile() calls take &str.

